.\" Made from the kstar help (src/help.rs); do not edit. See src/manual.rs.
.TH KSTAR-CHECK 1 "" "Kleene Star" "Kleene Star Manual"
.SH NAME
kstar\-check \- look for errors and warnings without running
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBkstar check\fR [options] <files>...
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Reports every error and warning in each program, without running it. A
folder means every .kstar file inside it.
.PP
The exit code is 0 when no file has errors (warnings do not count), 1 when
one has, and 2 when the command itself was wrong.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<when>\fR
auto (the default), always or never. With auto, output is coloured only on a terminal and never when the NO_COLOR environment variable is set.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBkstar check lab1.kstar\fR
check one program
.TP
\fBkstar check labs/\fR
check every program in labs/
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBkstar\fR(1),
\fBkstar\-help\fR(1)
.PP
The reference and the tutorial: https://github.com/Pratham71/kleene\-star
